<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sputnik 1</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1957">1957</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sputnik 1 was the first artificial Earth satellite, launched by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> from Baikonur on 4 October 1957. A polished sphere with four antennas, it transmitted radio signals for three weeks and burned up in the atmosphere in January 1958. Its launch shocked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and began the space race.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sputnik-1.jpg" alt="Sputnik 1" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Air Force photo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sputnik_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
